# NOTE: `src/lib/generated/selectInp.ts` is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# It is generated by `npm run gen:api` (`scripts/sync-declarations.mjs` copies it from
# `back/declarations/`), but it is a RUNTIME import, not a type-only one — see the
# `lesanApi` import at the top of `src/lib/client.ts`. So it is vendored source and
# must be committed, exactly like a checked-in protobuf/OpenAPI client.
#
# Ignoring it broke three things at once:
#   1. every fresh clone (`npm run typecheck`, `npm test` cannot resolve the module),
#   2. every EAS build — EAS uploads the working tree filtered by the `.gitignore`
#      files it finds, so the file never reached the build server and Metro failed
#      with "Unable to resolve module @/lib/generated/selectInp", which EAS surfaces
#      only as "Unknown error" in the Bundle JavaScript phase,
#   3. any CI running from a clean checkout.
#
# Regenerate with `npm run gen:api` and commit the result when the backend schema
# changes. Do not re-add an ignore rule for this path.

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

example

